  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2b524846",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Honestly, I find this really interesting.\n",
    "\n",
    "When I built this model before, I removed all punctuation marks because I thought they were unnecessary. I believed the model should be able to detect spam based on the meaning of the words alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "But here's the thing: `!!!` might appear in a spam advertisement, but someone could also write something like: \"Hey! Don't forget to turn off the stove!!!\"\n",
    "\n",
    "So, I can't just assume that punctuation marks are useless. I decided to keep them and investigate their impact.\n",
    "\n",
    "Interestingly, the model I trained while keeping punctuation marks achieved a higher F1 score. This doesn't necessarily prove that punctuation was the reason for the improvement, but it definitely makes it worth investigating further.\n",
    "\n",
    "Words like `the`, `to`, and `and` usually don't help much in distinguishing spam from normal emails.\n",
    "\n",
    "I think it's better to let TF-IDF handle these common words by using its stop-word filtering option, rather than removing them manually."
   ]
