   "id": "4ef98859",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "No image markers were detected in the processed `Message` column.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, all 217 emails containing emojis turned out to be spam. At first, this looks like an amazing feature for separating spam from normal emails. But the more I think about it, the more worried I get. Maybe it could cause the model to overfit.\n",
    "\n",
    "Not because there are too few emails with emojis, but because every single email containing emojis is spam. The model might simply learn that any email with an emoji must be spam.\n",
    "\n",
    "Of course, these observations apply only to this version of the dataset, and I need to test the feature's impact on the model.\n"
   ]
