   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Training the Main Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Following the standard approach I've learned so far, I need to split the data into training and test sets.\n",
    "\n",
    "But this time, I'm also creating a validation set because I'll need it to choose some of the model's parameters.\n",
    "\n",
    "I'm also using `GroupShuffleSplit` instead of a regular train-test split. This is to make sure duplicate emails don't end up in both the training and test sets.\n",
    "\n",
    "First, I split the data into two groups and set one aside for testing. Then I split the remaining data again into training and validation sets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 43,
   "id": "47eb058c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = data.drop(columns=[\"Spam/Ham\", \"char_count\", \"row_id\"], errors=\"ignore\")\n",
    "y = data[\"Spam/Ham\"]\n",
    "groups = X[\"Message\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "split1 = GroupShuffleSplit(\n",
    "    n_splits=1,\n",
    "    test_size=0.18,\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "train_val_idx, test_idx = next(\n",
    "    split1.split(X, y, groups)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_temp = X.iloc[train_val_idx].copy()\n",
    "X_test = X.iloc[test_idx].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "y_temp = y.iloc[train_val_idx].copy()\n",
    "y_test = y.iloc[test_idx].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "split2 = GroupShuffleSplit(\n",
    "    n_splits=1,\n",
    "    test_size=0.12,\n",
    "    random_state=42\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "train_idx, val_idx = next(\n",
    "    split2.split(X_temp, y_temp, groups.iloc[train_val_idx])\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train = X_temp.iloc[train_idx].copy()\n",
    "X_val = X_temp.iloc[val_idx].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train = y_temp.iloc[train_idx].copy()\n",
    "y_val = y_temp.iloc[val_idx].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "train_groups = groups.iloc[train_val_idx].iloc[train_idx].copy()\n"
   ]
  },
