    "Still, LinearSVC is generally good at working with datasets that have a large number of features, especially high-dimensional text data.\n",
    "\n",
    "It also uses a linear decision boundary, so maybe our data can be separated quite well using a linear boundary.\n",
    "\n",
    "Of course, these are just some possible reasons why LinearSVC performed better.\n",
    "\n",
    "The comparison is not fully balanced because only LinearSVC received hyperparameter tuning. I'll treat the other two models as baselines rather than using this comparison as proof that LinearSVC is universally better.\n",
