   "source": [
    "The results show that adding numerical features to TF-IDF made only a very small difference in overall performance.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **All Features:** Achieved an average F1-score of 0.989949.\n",
    "- **Without `url_count`:** Achieved 0.989990, slightly higher than the All Features configuration.\n",
    "- **Without `emoji`:** Achieved 0.990030, the highest average F1-score among all experiments.\n",
    "- **`log_char_count`:** Adding this feature improved the average F1-score compared with TF-IDF alone (0.989989 vs. 0.989833).\n",
    "- **`url_count`:** Adding or removing this feature had almost no effect on the average F1-score.\n",
    "- **`emoji` and `word_count`:** Neither feature produced a meaningful improvement over TF-IDF alone.\n",
    "\n",
    "The difference between the highest and lowest average F1-scores is approximately 0.000279. The standard deviations across the five folds range from approximately 0.001265 to 0.001628.\n",
    "\n",
    "These differences are very small compared with the variation across folds. Therefore, there is insufficient evidence to conclude that any of the feature configurations consistently outperforms the others.\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, the numerical features provided little additional benefit over TF-IDF alone. Although `log_char_count` showed a small improvement, the results suggest that TF-IDF already captures most of the useful information for this classification task."
   ]
  },
